SKIP – The class is a thin wrapper around CompletableFuture and AtomicReference that mainly forwards calls to existing concurrency primitives. Its logic consists of simple state updates and method delegations, which are already well‑optimized in the JDK and RxJava core. There is no computationally intensive algorithm or complex control flow that would benefit from micro‑benchmarking with JMH. Consequently, writing a dedicated JMH benchmark would provide little insight beyond what standard unit tests already verify.